## Quick Reference

| Action | Command |
|--------|---------|
| Start phase | `git checkout main && git pull && git checkout -b phase-N-name` |
| Commit work | `git add . && git commit -m "Description"` |
| Push branch | `git push origin phase-N-name` |
| Create PR | `gh pr create --base main --head phase-N-name` |
| After merge | `git checkout main && git pull` |
| Tag release | `git tag -a v1.0.0 -m "Release" && git push origin v1.0.0` |

## Summary

**Always start from `main`**  
**One phase = One branch**  
**Merge before starting next phase**  
**Keep history clean and linear**
